  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(0,-7)$ and $(6,1)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Find the radius of the circle.",
  "worked_solution": "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0-6)}^{2}+{(-7-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5\n$$",
